{"availability":"available","full":"hanabi/hanabi.github.io","name":"hanabi.github.io","description":"A list of Hanabi strategies","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":186,"forks":195,"created":"2018-02-21T07:34:18Z","updated":"2026-10-06T10:37:45Z","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hanabi.github.io/","topics":[],"demo":"https://hanabi.github.io/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:12.219Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:12.219Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:12.219Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:56.318Z","stars":186,"forks":195},{"at":"2026-10-09T05:49:12.219Z","stars":186,"forks":195}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is the GitHub repository for the website. It is built with Docusaurus, a modern static website generator.","If you're in the H-Group, then you might want to help edit the website. Maybe you want to fix some typos. Or maybe you want to add a new example. Or maybe you proposed a new convention, and it got voted in, and now you need to add a new section. Regardless of what you are doing, you will need to submit a pull request.","In plain English, a pull request (or a PR for short) is simply a request to merge the changes that you want into the main copy of the website. Essentially, you need to make a copy of the website (called a fork), make some changes (called a commit), and then click a button on the website to create a new PR. At that point, I'll be notified that there is a new PR and I can look over the specific changes. Then, I can click \"Approve\" or \"Deny\" accordingly. If I click \"Approve\", then the changes are integrated and the website is automatically updated!"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hanabi/hanabi.github.io/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5ba91a3bc16e63eb18b7604aa36382b373b90eec28244115afe2ec584a05edd7","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:56.478Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-1